<title>SPAIN: Spain's Rojo urges European social spending fall.</title>
<headline>Spain's Rojo urges European social spending fall.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of Spain governor Luis Angel Rojo on Friday called again for a reduction in social spending if European economic and monetary union targets are to be met.</p>
<p>The central bank governor said rising social costs were &quot;the most substantial obstacle to the progress of the European integration project.&quot;</p>
<p>Rojo told a seminar in Santander: &quot;European economies will have difficulty getting into a phase of higher sustained growth while the great problem of their high and persistent public deficits are not tackled. Growing social expenses have an important, but not unique, role in these deficits.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
</text>
